## Phase 2: Reorganize `D:\My Drive\Sync\Config\omniroute` (Mixed Data)

**Goal:** Keep essential data in Drive sync, move caches/logs to local, use junctions to link them.

### Step 2.1: Identify Current C: Drive Junctions
Document which C: paths point to `D:\My Drive\Sync\Config\omniroute`.

### Step 2.2: Prepare Local Structure
```
D:\My System\Local App Junction\OmniRoute\Config\
├── call_logs\           (2.9GB - runtime, non-essential)
├── logs\                (101MB - runtime, non-essential)
├── qoder-cli\           (2.2GB - cache, non-essential)
├── server\              (15B - PID file, non-essential)
└── supervisor\          (10B - PID file, non-essential)
```

### Step 2.3: Move Non-Essential Items
1. Copy non-essential folders to `D:\My System\Local App Junction\OmniRoute\Config\`
2. Delete originals from `D:\My Drive\Sync\Config\omniroute\`
3. Create junctions in `D:\My Drive\Sync\Config\omniroute\` pointing back:

```batch
mklink /J "D:\My Drive\Sync\Config\omniroute\call_logs" "D:\My System\Local App Junction\OmniRoute\Config\call_logs"
mklink /J "D:\My Drive\Sync\Config\omniroute\logs" "D:\My System\Local App Junction\OmniRoute\Config\logs"
mklink /J "D:\My Drive\Sync\Config\omniroute\qoder-cli" "D:\My System\Local App Junction\OmniRoute\Config\qoder-cli"
mklink /J "D:\My Drive\Sync\Config\omniroute\server" "D:\My System\Local App Junction\OmniRoute\Config\server"
mklink /J "D:\My Drive\Sync\Config\omniroute\supervisor" "D:\My System\Local App Junction\OmniRoute\Config\supervisor"
```

### Step 2.4: Essential Items Remain (NO Junctions)
These stay directly in Drive-synced folder:
- `storage.sqlite` (757MB - user data)
- `oauth/` (36B - credentials)
- `.env` (140B - user config)
- `db_backups/` (299KB - backups)
- `omniroute_config_*.py` (14KB - config tools)

### Step 2.5: Update C: Drive Junctions
For each C: junction pointing to `D:\My Drive\Sync\Config\omniroute`:
- Keep junction path same (points to `D:\My Drive\Sync\Config\omniroute`)
- It now auto-routes through the new junction structure

### Step 2.6: Verify
- Application can write to call_logs, logs, qoder-cli (through junctions)
- storage.sqlite is directly editable (no junction interference)
- All C: drive paths work as before

